             {
                "text": "#### What about inside us?\n\nWe have seen enormous numbers in the age of the universe and the count of stars. But surprisingly, enormous numbers also exist inside us - at the tiniest scale imaginable.\n\nInside everything - your hand, a leaf, a drop of water - there are incredibly small elements called atoms. Atoms are so small that a single grain of sand contains more atoms than there are grains of sand on all of Earth's beaches.",
